rook: Keep the Bluetooth controller awake

The Bluetooth HAL turns on the BCM43569's sleep mode, where the host has to
assert BT_WAKE before each command. Nothing can on the Spot: its devicetree
has no wake GPIO and the kernel no bluesleep. A command sent once the
controller had dozed off was never answered, so the stack timed out and
restarted Bluetooth, every time Kiosk Satellite's Bluetooth proxy started a
scan after a quiet spell. The Spot runs on mains power, so the controller
now stays awake.

